["<aside class=\"callout warn\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Warning</div><p>Study aid only. The law is the law. If a change could alter your rifle's legal class, ask a qualified gunsmith and the RCMP (Royal Canadian Mounted Police) Canadian Firearms Program first.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 362\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"How the CZ 457 barrel swap works, exploded side view: 1 two barrel screws under the front of the receiver hold the barrel, 2 the barrel shank slides into the receiver, 3 the receiver, which is the part the law treats as the firearm, 4 the barrel; CZ offers .22 LR, .22 WMR and .17 HMR. The stock comes off first. Have a gunsmith check headspace.\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"362\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">The barrel swap system</text><rect x=\"40\" y=\"90\" width=\"150\" height=\"40\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#4A5156\"/><rect x=\"160\" y=\"96\" width=\"30\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#2B3034\"/><rect x=\"230\" y=\"98\" width=\"40\" height=\"24\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#8C959B\"/><path d=\"M268 100 L392 104 L392 116 L268 120 Z\" fill=\"#4A5156\"/><circle cx=\"166\" cy=\"136\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#D8B23A\" stroke=\"#2B3034\"/><circle cx=\"184\" cy=\"136\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#D8B23A\" stroke=\"#2B3034\"/><line x1=\"226\" y1=\"110\" x2=\"209.0\" y2=\"110.0\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><path d=\"M198 110 L209.0 116.0 L209.0 104.0z\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><circle cx=\"175\" cy=\"168\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"175\" y=\"173\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">1</text><line x1=\"170\" y1=\"158\" x2=\"166\" y2=\"142\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><line x1=\"180\" y1=\"158\" x2=\"184\" y2=\"142\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"72\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"250\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">2</text><line x1=\"250\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"250\" y2=\"98\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"72\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">3</text><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"90\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"72\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"77\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">4</text><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"104\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"209\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">1</text><text x=\"42\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Two barrel screws, under the front</text><circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"233\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">2</text><text x=\"42\" y=\"238\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Barrel shank slides into the receiver</text><circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"257\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">3</text><text x=\"42\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Receiver: the part the law counts</text><circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"281\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">4</text><text x=\"42\" y=\"286\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Barrel: .22 LR, .22 WMR, .17 HMR kits</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"316\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"338.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">Stock off first. Headspace: gunsmith check.</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Two screws hold the barrel in the receiver <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li>CZ: barrel and calibre change \"at the highest user level\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: how the system works</summary><ul><li>\"Modular system allowing barrel replacement and calibre change at the highest user level\" (95%, CZ manual page 4).</li><li>\"The receiver, in which only two front screws retain the barrel, allows for quick and easy barrel changing ... simply remove the receiver from the stock and you'll see the two screws that secure the barrel\" (80%, all4shooters test, 2020).</li><li>The parts list names them \"Barrel Screw (2x)\", part 2 (95%, CZ manual page 12).</li><li>Kits: \"CZ's simple barrel change system enables caliber conversion to .17 HMR and .22 Winchester Magnum\" (80%, all4shooters). HMR means Hornady Magnum Rimfire; WMR means Winchester Magnum Rimfire.</li><li>Each calibre needs its own magazine; a bolt or extractor change may also be needed: <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> with CZ or your dealer before buying a kit.</li><li>Barrels and magazines also fit the CZ 455 (95%, page 4).</li></ul></details>","<div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Pros</th><th>Cons</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>You, at home</td><td>Cheap, quick (Tip)</td><td>CZ's stripping page says go no further than the bolt <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></td></tr><tr><td>Gunsmith</td><td>Headspace checked, screws torqued (Tip)</td><td>Costs a bench fee (<span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span>)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class=\"callout lean\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">My lean (opinion)</div><p>My lean: first swap at a gunsmith, and ask them to check headspace. Watch, then decide.</p></aside><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: why a gunsmith first</summary><ul><li>The manual's caution: \"Do not strip your firearm any further ... entrust this work to a competent gunsmith\" (95%, page 9). Taking the stock off and loosening barrel screws goes past bolt removal (90%, my reading).</li><li>Owners report stuck barrels and lost small parts when the receiver came apart (55%, forum reports: Tip only).</li><li>Headspace is the fit between the bolt face and the chamber; aftermarket barrels may need shims and gauges (60%, barrel shim maker listing). Factory CZ barrels are meant to drop in (80%, all4shooters).</li><li>Stock screws back to 3.5 Nm after (95%, CZ page 9).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 314\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four lines you must not cross with a CZ 457 in Canada: a suppressor or silencer is a prohibited device; making it fire more than one shot per trigger pull makes it an automatic, a prohibited firearm; cutting the barrel or rifle down so the barrel is under 457 mm, or the rifle under 660 mm, makes an adapted prohibited firearm; a bullpup stock is a prohibited device. Criminal Code section 84 and SOR/98-462.\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"314\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Lines you must not cross</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"44\" width=\"372\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"67\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><line x1=\"31\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"74\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"45\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"31\" y2=\"74\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Suppressor (silencer)</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Prohibited device</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"98\" width=\"372\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"121\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><line x1=\"31\" y1=\"114\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"128\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"45\" y1=\"114\" x2=\"31\" y2=\"128\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Make it fire more than once</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Automatic: prohibited</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"152\" width=\"372\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"175\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><line x1=\"31\" y1=\"168\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"45\" y1=\"168\" x2=\"31\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Cut the barrel under 457 mm</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"191\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Adapted: prohibited</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"206\" width=\"372\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"229\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><line x1=\"31\" y1=\"222\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"236\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"45\" y1=\"222\" x2=\"31\" y2=\"236\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Bullpup stock</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Prohibited device</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Criminal Code s. 84 and SOR/98-462 (95 to 99%).</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"302\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Unsure? Ask a gunsmith and the RCMP CFP.</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>The receiver is the firearm. A barrel is a \"firearm part\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>Cut a rifle under 660 mm, or its barrel under 457 mm: prohibited <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the legal text and what it means for you</summary><aside class=\"callout law\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Criminal Code s. 84(1), \"prohibited firearm\" (b)</div><p>\"a firearm that is adapted from a rifle or shotgun, whether by sawing, cutting or any other alteration, and that, as so adapted, (i) is less than 660 mm in length, or (ii) is 660 mm or greater in length and has a barrel less than 457 mm in length\"</p></aside><ul><li>Plain English: never shorten your CZ or its barrel below those numbers <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>\"Restricted firearm\" includes one with a barrel under 470 mm that fires centre fire ammunition semi automatically (99%, s. 84(1)). Your bolt action rimfire is not that (95%, my reading).</li><li>\"Firearm part means a barrel for a firearm\" (99%, s. 84(1)). \"Firearm\" includes \"any frame or receiver\" (99%, s. 2).</li><li>A factory barrel shorter than 457 mm swapped onto a rifle that came longer: could that be \"any other alteration\"? Not answered here. <span class=\"verify\">VERIFY</span> with the RCMP Canadian Firearms Program before you buy one (Tip: keep barrels at 457 mm or longer).</li><li>BC hunting: no firearm with a barrel under 305 mm (99%, synopsis page 12).</li><li>Text current to 30 September 2026, read 2026-10-23.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 388\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The CZ 457 trigger adjustment screws from the manual, Figs. 6 and 7: screw A sets the pull weight and screw B the travel after the shot, both reached with the stock removed; screw C in the trigger sets the travel before the shot. After any change, do the safety check: the rifle must not fire.\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"388\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Trigger screws A, B, C</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"44\" width=\"376\" height=\"190\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"120\" y=\"60\" width=\"150\" height=\"70\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#4A5156\"/><path d=\"M190 130 Q210 170 180 206\" stroke=\"#8C959B\" stroke-width=\"10\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"96\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#D8B23A\" stroke=\"#2B3034\"/><circle cx=\"150\" cy=\"118\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#D8B23A\" stroke=\"#2B3034\"/><circle cx=\"196\" cy=\"160\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#D8B23A\" stroke=\"#2B3034\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"101\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FF6A13\">A</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"123\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FF6A13\">B</text><text x=\"232\" y=\"166\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FF6A13\">C</text><line x1=\"108\" y1=\"96\" x2=\"142\" y2=\"96\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"108\" y1=\"118\" x2=\"142\" y2=\"118\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"224\" y1=\"162\" x2=\"202\" y2=\"160\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"257\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">A</text><text x=\"42\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Pull weight (stock off)</text><circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"283\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">B</text><text x=\"42\" y=\"288\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Travel after the shot (stock off)</text><circle cx=\"26\" cy=\"309\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">C</text><text x=\"42\" y=\"314\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Travel before the shot (in the trigger)</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"342\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"364.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">Then the safety check. It must not fire.</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>A: pull weight. B: travel after the shot. Both with the stock off <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>C, in the trigger: travel before the shot <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the manual's words</summary><ul><li>\"The adjustment of the trigger pull and trigger travel distance after firing (Fig. 6) is performed with the shoulder stock removed, using set screws A (pull) and B (travel after firing). The trigger travel distance before firing can be set using screw C positioned in the trigger (Fig. 7)\" (95%, CZ manual page 7).</li><li>Parts list: 53 trigger pull setting screw (A), 51 trigger dead travel screw (B), 49 trigger setting screw (C) (95%, page 12).</li><li>Stock off means the stock screws come out: 3.5 Nm on reassembly (95%, page 9).</li><li>My lean: let a gunsmith set it the first time (Tip). CZ's caution on further stripping applies (95%, page 9).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 308\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"CZ 457 trigger pull ranges from the manual. Standard trigger: adjustable 8 to 15 newtons, set at the factory to 11.1 to 14 newtons. Comfort trigger: 5 to 7 newtons, factory 6 newtons give or take 0.5. 4.45 newtons is about 1 pound. Stay inside the range.\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"308\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Trigger pull: the CZ ranges</text><line x1=\"40.0\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"40.0\" y2=\"210\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"40.0\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">4</text><line x1=\"95.0\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"95.0\" y2=\"210\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"95.0\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">6</text><line x1=\"150.0\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"150.0\" y2=\"210\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"150.0\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">8</text><line x1=\"205.0\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"205.0\" y2=\"210\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"205.0\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">10</text><line x1=\"260.0\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"260.0\" y2=\"210\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"260.0\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">12</text><line x1=\"315.0\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"315.0\" y2=\"210\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"315.0\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">14</text><line x1=\"370.0\" y1=\"58\" x2=\"370.0\" y2=\"210\" stroke=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"370.0\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">16</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"246\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#17201A\">newtons (N); 4.45 N = 1 lb</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Standard: 8 to 15 N</text><rect x=\"150.0\" y=\"80\" width=\"192.5\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\"/><rect x=\"235.2\" y=\"80\" width=\"79.8\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"40\" y=\"124\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Factory: 11.1 to 14 N (dark)</text><text x=\"40\" y=\"152\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Comfort: 5 to 7 N</text><rect x=\"67.5\" y=\"162\" width=\"55.0\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#D9E0D5\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\"/><rect x=\"81.2\" y=\"162\" width=\"27.5\" height=\"22\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\"/><text x=\"133.5\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Factory 6 N, give or take 0.5</text><rect x=\"8\" y=\"262\" width=\"384\" height=\"34\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"284.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\">Stay inside the range. Never lighter.</text></svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Standard: 8 to 15 N, factory 11.1 to 14 N <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Comfort: 5 to 7 N, factory 6 N <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: limits, the safety check and the law</summary><ul><li>\"The standard trigger mechanism enables setting the trigger pull in the range of 8-15 N (the trigger pull is set by the manufacturer in the safe range of 11.1-14 N)\" (95%, CZ manual page 7).</li><li>\"The Comfort trigger mechanism enables setting the trigger pull in the range of 5-7 N (... 6 ± 0.5 N)\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>In pounds: 8 to 15 N is about 1.8 to 3.4 lb, matching CZ USA's \"1.8 to 3.4 lbs\" (95%, conversion; 85% CZ USA page).</li><li>\"Do not set the trigger pull too low and the trigger travel too short because the rifle could unintentionally discharge a cartridge when being handled improperly\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Safety check on the unloaded rifle: open and close the bolt repeatedly, move the safety on and off; \"the rifle must not discharge\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Law: a trigger that fires more than once per pull makes an \"automatic firearm\", which is a prohibited firearm (99%, Criminal Code s. 84(1)). Bump fire or trigger devices for semi automatics are prohibited devices too (99%, SOR/98-462 Part 4 s. 1).</li><li>For a hunting rifle, light is not better: stay in the factory range (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 314\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four lines you must not cross with a CZ 457 in Canada: a suppressor or silencer is a prohibited device; making it fire more than one shot per trigger pull makes it an automatic, a prohibited firearm; cutting the barrel or rifle down so the barrel is under 457 mm, or the rifle under 660 mm, makes an adapted prohibited firearm; a bullpup stock is a prohibited device. Criminal Code section 84 and SOR/98-462.\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"314\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/><text x=\"200\" y=\"27\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Lines you must not cross</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"44\" width=\"372\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"67\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><line x1=\"31\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"74\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"45\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"31\" y2=\"74\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"64\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Suppressor (silencer)</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"83\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Prohibited device</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"98\" width=\"372\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"121\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><line x1=\"31\" y1=\"114\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"128\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"45\" y1=\"114\" x2=\"31\" y2=\"128\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Make it fire more than once</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"137\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Automatic: prohibited</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"152\" width=\"372\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"175\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><line x1=\"31\" y1=\"168\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"45\" y1=\"168\" x2=\"31\" y2=\"182\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Cut the barrel under 457 mm</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"191\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Adapted: prohibited</text><rect x=\"14\" y=\"206\" width=\"372\" height=\"46\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"38\" cy=\"229\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#FF6A13\"/><line x1=\"31\" y1=\"222\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"236\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><line x1=\"45\" y1=\"222\" x2=\"31\" y2=\"236\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"226\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Bullpup stock</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"245\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Prohibited device</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"normal\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#17201A\">Criminal Code s. 84 and SOR/98-462 (95 to 99%).</text><text x=\"16\" y=\"302\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\">Unsure? Ask a gunsmith and the RCMP CFP.</text></svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): If a change makes you ask \"is this legal?\", stop and ask someone who knows, in writing.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Shortening a barrel because it \"looks handier\". That can make a prohibited firearm.</li><li>Setting the trigger below the range and skipping the safety check.</li><li>Buying a .22 WMR barrel and using .22 LR magazines.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Write down your trigger setting and barrel calibre on a card in the case. Ask your gunsmith to sign the date.</p></aside>","<ul><li>CZ 457 manual pages 4, 7, 9, 12 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>. Criminal Code ss. 2 and 84, SOR/98-462 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>. all4shooters <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>. Forum reports (Tip). Checked 2026-10-23.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: all sources</summary><ul><li><a href=\"https://czubpimstorage.blob.core.windows.net/strapi-pim/assets/735342000443_CZ_457_05_2025_en_es_cs_de_fr_8dc25ceb9d.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CZ 457 instruction manual, 05 2025 (PDF)</a>: page 4 (modular barrels), page 7 (trigger adjustment, ranges, safety check, Figs. 6 and 7), page 9 (caution, stock screws), page 12 (parts 2, 49, 51, 53). Read directly 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/C-46/section-84.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Criminal Code s. 84</a> (automatic firearm, firearm part, prohibited device, prohibited firearm, restricted firearm) and <a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/C-46/section-2.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">s. 2</a> (firearm), current to 30 September 2026, read directly 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://laws-lois.justice.gc.ca/eng/regulations/SOR-98-462/FullText.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SOR/98-462, Part 4</a>, current to 30 September 2026, read directly 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.all4shooters.com/en/shooting/rifles/cz-457-three-new-rimfire-synthetic-thumbhole-and-long-range-precision-threaded-test/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">all4shooters CZ 457 test, 2020</a> <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">80%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.czfirearms.com/en-us/products/rimfire-rifles/cz-457-series/cz-457-american\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">CZ USA: CZ 457 American</a>: trigger 1.8 to 3.4 lb <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li><a href=\"https://www.longrangehunting.com/threads/issues-with-the-cz457-switch-barrel.344012/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Long Range Hunting forum: issues with the CZ 457 switch barrel</a> and <a href=\"https://eabco.com/cz-455-457-barrel-shim-kit/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">EABCO barrel shim kit</a>: owner reports and shims (55 to 60%, Tip only).</li><li>Synopsis 2026 to 2028 page 12, barrel under 305 mm, via <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods\">legal methods</a> <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li></ul></details>"]